CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
Control for `store_through_pointer_if_element`: with i in {0, 1}, main's
`*r = 5` may really store to items[0] after the thread's store of 1. The
element actually stored must still be published, so this must stay FAILED
before and after.
